# The journal is append-only and is written by two different operating systems:
# Frank's Windows machine and the Ubuntu runner. Pin the data files to LF in
# both the repo and the working tree, or a Windows checkout rewrites every line
# ending and each hourly commit shows the entire file as changed.
*.jsonl text eol=lf
*.py    text eol=lf
*.yml   text eol=lf

# Append-only data: use git's built-in union merge.
#
# Both runners now write - the hosted workflow and Frank's local Claude cron -
# and on 2026-09-02 that produced add/add conflicts on seven data files. The
# only correct resolution for an append-only log is BOTH sides: picking one
# deletes rows that really were collected. `merge=union` is built into git, so
# it needs no local config to work on a fresh clone or on the runner.
#
# Order and duplicates do not matter here: every row is self-contained and
# timestamped, readers sort as needed, and outcomes dedupe on (pair, horizon).
*.jsonl merge=union
